* C4 variant full (RSpice-authored; corpus design C4): the testbench tb_sar
* drives the register's clk and start (digital nets the two modules share) and
* watches eoc and the bits on their analog nodes. NCONV is the number of
* conversions before $finish; the decks set it to their staircase length.
xtb clk start eoc b7 b6 b5 b4 b3 b2 b1 b0 tb_sar NCONV={nconv}
xsar clk start cmp samp eoc b7 b6 b5 b4 b3 b2 b1 b0 sar8
